WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.999
Measure power draw at idle, startup, model load, prompt processing, and sustained generation.

00:00:05.999 --> 00:00:10.990
Capacity planning includes GPU, CPU, drives, fans, power conversion, room cooling,

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.258
circuit limits, and future hardware.

00:00:13.258 --> 00:00:18.703
Monitor GPU memory, utilization, temperature, clocks, power, errors, fan speed, host memory,

00:00:18.703 --> 00:00:21.879
disk, queue depth, latency, and process health.

00:00:21.879 --> 00:00:25.509
Per-device visibility helps reveal imbalance and stalled work.

00:00:25.509 --> 00:00:30.500
Logs should preserve model, runtime, driver, device assignment, split, context, batch,

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.584
request outcome, and failure without retaining sensitive prompts unnecessarily.

00:00:34.584 --> 00:00:37.306
Configuration records make performance changes explainable.

00:00:37.306 --> 00:00:39.575
Crash recovery needs defined behavior.

00:00:39.575 --> 00:00:44.566
Decide whether services restart, requests retry, models reload on remaining devices,

00:00:44.566 --> 00:00:46.835
or the system fails closed.

00:00:46.835 --> 00:00:50.919
Test recovery before assuming one extra GPU provides redundancy.

00:00:50.919 --> 00:00:55.910
Physical setup requires secure cards, supported cables, clear airflow, stable mounting,

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.178
safe power, and restricted access.

00:00:58.178 --> 00:01:00.901
High-temperature surfaces, spinning fans, heavy cards,

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:04.077
and improvised open frames require appropriate controls.

00:01:04.077 --> 00:01:09.522
Maintenance includes dust removal, filter inspection, cable and fan checks, thermal review,

00:01:09.522 --> 00:01:12.698
driver patching, storage cleanup, and benchmark regression.

00:01:12.698 --> 00:01:16.782
Operational reliability matters more than a one-time record score.

00:01:16.782 --> 00:01:19.958
An extra GPU is not automatic redundancy.

00:01:19.958 --> 00:01:23.588
A shared power supply, host, storage device, driver,

00:01:23.588 --> 00:01:26.764
or runtime can still stop every workload.

00:01:26.764 --> 00:01:29.940
Test component and service failure behavior explicitly.
